---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Search a run's events for one or more substrings (all must match).

A term is matched against the text an event carries: log output, an assertion's
message and source function, and a test-composer command.

Each matching event has its moment (an input_hash and a vtime), its source, and
its payload. To stream the logs of an event's timeline to its current end, pass
its run ID and input_hash to `snouty runs logs <run_id> <hash>`.

Matching events print as classified blocks: a `moment HASH` divider opens each
timeline segment, and each event below it renders on one line in the Antithesis
event shapes — SDK assertions, faults, container lifecycle, test composer — each
in their own concise form.

Matching runs server-side through the events-search API, the same route
`snouty runs search` takes. Every term must match, case-insensitively. The
result is a sample of the matching events in no fixed order, capped at --limit.
Read `snouty runs search --help` to learn how to read a sample and how the run's
timelines relate the events.

The run must be ready or complete. If it is not, the command waits until it is
ready, as `snouty runs exec` does, and says that it waits.

The command needs tenant release 62.2 or newer; `snouty doctor` reports the
tenant release.

For log output, the equivalent search is:
  snouty runs search <run_id> \
    'filter(ev => ["a", "b"].every(t =>
      (ev.output_text || "").toLowerCase().includes(t)))'
with each term in lower case. `snouty --verbose runs events ...` prints the
exact query, which also matches assertion messages and test-composer commands.

Examples:
  snouty runs events <run_id> -m error
  snouty runs events <run_id> -m error -m node-0 -n 100

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each event prints as one JSON object on
its own line:
  snouty --json runs events <run_id> -m error | jq -r .moment.vtime

Usage: snouty runs events [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID> [QUERY]...

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

  [QUERY]...
          Substrings to match, as a positional alias for `-m` (all must match).
          At least one needle (via `-m` or here) is required

Options:
  -m, --match <MATCHES>
          Substring to search for (repeatable; all matches must be present)

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of events to print, at most 999. Raise it to make a
          search more exhaustive
          
          [default: 50]

  -d, --detail
          Detailed rendering: a full-width vtime on every line, source
          locations, and each event's attached details JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
